     fhir:div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n            <p>This code system \n              <code>http://hl7.org/fhir/map-target-list-mode</code> defines the following codes:\n            </p>\n            <table class=\"codes\">\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">\n                  <b>Code</b>\n                </td>\n                <td>\n                  <b>Display</b>\n                </td>\n                <td>\n                  <b>Definition</b>\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">first\n                  <a name=\"map-target-list-mode-first\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>First</td>\n                <td>when the target list is being assembled, the items for this rule go first. If more than one rule defines a first item (for a given instance of mapping) then this is an error.</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">share\n                  <a name=\"map-target-list-mode-share\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>Share</td>\n                <td>the target instance is shared with the target instances generated by another rule (up to the first common n items, then create new ones).</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">last\n                  <a name=\"map-target-list-mode-last\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>Last</td>\n                <td>when the target list is being assembled, the items for this rule go last. If more than one rule defines a last item (for a given instance of mapping) then this is an error.</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">single\n                  <a name=\"map-target-list-mode-single\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>single</td>\n                <td>the target instance is shared with a number of target instances generated by another rule (up to the first common n items, then create new ones).</td>\n              </tr>\n            </table>\n          </div>"^^rdf:XMLLiteral
