  fhir:text [
     fhir:status [ fhir:v "generated" ] ;
     fhir:div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n            <p>This code system \n              <code>http://hl7.org/fhir/task-intent</code> defines the following codes:\n            </p>\n            <table class=\"codes\">\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">\n                  <b>Code</b>\n                </td>\n                <td>\n                  <b>Display</b>\n                </td>\n                <td>\n                  <b>Definition</b>\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">unknown\n                  <a name=\"task-intent-unknown\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>Unknown</td>\n                <td>The intent is not known.  When dealing with Task, it's not always known (or relevant) how the task was initiated - i.e. whether it was proposed, planned, ordered or just done spontaneously.</td>\n              </tr>\n            </table>\n          </div>"^^rdf:XMLLiteral
